  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="5aa3e5d4-7472-5bbf-a973-61121693e413" activityNameId="c512b246-55d0-5f04-bd01-71f7fb60d747" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Pedestrian underpass, underneath 2 tracks</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Pedestrian underpass, underneath 2 tracks
A standard pedestrian underpass was considered, which crosses under a double track. The pedestrian underpass itself is 4 metres wide and 20 metres long. There is a staircase (3 m x 23 m) and a ramp (3 m x 33 m) on both sides. In total (including stairs and ramps), the area of such a pedestrian underpass is 416m2. For larger (under 3 or more tracks) pedestrian underpasses, it is assumed that the materialisation per m2 is similar, as an additional ramp and stairs are normally required even with additional tracks. The data for the material requirements of the pedestrian underpass comes from SBB (pers. comm. SBB, 2019) and was used for an indication of the average material requirements per m2. Offcuts and rejects are not taken into account. It is assumed that the excavated material will be used elsewhere on site and will not be deposited. The energy requirement for the construction work (excluding excavation) was derived from an LCA study by SBB on the construction of a platform per tonne of installed material (Rüegsegger &amp; Schori, 2017). The ecoinvent standard values were used for transport distances for material deliveries by lorry (Frischknecht et al., 2007).

According to SBB, the service life of such a pedestrian underpass is 78 years. Only the surface layer (surfacing) is expected to last 30 years (pers. comm., SBB, 2024). Maintenance work, refurbishment and dismantling of the pedestrian underpass are not taken into account.; UUID:cc35c5b9-2d9d-3972-a31c-a8b23a4055bb
The inventory includes all the materials, energy and transport necessary for constructing a pedestrian underpass underneath 2 railway tracks. Excluded are maintenance and disposal
Location: Data apply to construction in Switzerland. 
Technology: Average technology available on the market
Time period: Time of publications.
Production volume: 
Sampling: based on literature 
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_cc35c5b9-2d9d-3972-a31c-a8b23a4055bb.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
